# Repository-wide line-ending policy.
#
# Goal: every text file is LF in BOTH the index and the working copy,
# on every platform. This makes contributor `core.autocrlf` settings
# irrelevant — Windows / macOS / Linux / CI all see identical bytes —
# and stops the "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches
# it" warning that fires when files written by tools like Vitest's
# snapshot writer are read back on a Windows checkout configured with
# `core.autocrlf=true`.
#
# Toolchain confirmed LF-clean: pnpm, vite, vitest, biome, lit,
# Tauri, Storybook. CI runs on Linux.
#
# Override per-pattern below if a file genuinely needs CRLF (no such
# files in this repo today — Windows shell scripts like `.bat` /
# `.cmd` / `.ps1` are not tracked).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files. Auto-detection works for these, but pinning the
# attribute prevents a future contributor / tool from accidentally
# treating them as text and corrupting the bytes.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.wasm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
